# What a PHP consumer of `coolms/theme-admin` receives.
#
# Composer serves a git archive, so anything tracked and not excluded here is
# downloaded by every application that installs this package. The Angular
# sources are 480 of the 1146 tracked files and 5.60 of the 26.67 MB, and a PHP
# application can do nothing with them: building the admin needs Node, an
# Angular toolchain and roughly 837 MB of node_modules. They belong in the
# repository and not in the package.
#
# !! THE FIGURES ABOVE WERE RE-MEASURED 2026-09-07 and they had drifted. The
# previous ones -- 502 of 516 files, 13.25 of 13.70 MB -- were true when written
# and stopped being true when 2.0.0-alpha4 put the built admin in the package.
# The tree roughly doubled and `angular/` stopped being the bulk of it, so the
# sentence justifying this exclusion was arguing from numbers that no longer
# reproduced.
#
# !! `export-ignore` affects the ARCHIVE ONLY. Everything below stays in git,
# stays in CI, and stays in a clone. Nothing is being deleted.
#
# !! `tests/` IS KEPT, and the exception that used to exclude it is withdrawn.
# The argument for it was that percentages of a 21 MB archive are real
# megabytes. Measured, the whole of `tests/` is one 3,581-byte file, and adding
# it to the archive changes the file count from 661 to 662 and the byte count
# not at all -- it fits inside tar's existing block padding. Zero bytes is not
# a percentage worth an exception, so the estate rule stands here too: tests
# ship, because someone debugging an integration reads them.
angular/          export-ignore
phpunit.xml.dist  export-ignore
.github/          export-ignore
package-lock.json export-ignore
.gitattributes    export-ignore
